Credit for the original implementation and the original test suite belongs to that
project and its contributors.

The correspondence was traced against neo4j/cypher-dsl at commit d3b17e42, one commit
after release 2025.3.6. Only that state was traced; material added upstream after it is
not claimed.

Where the code corresponds

  src/cypher_dsl/render/        rendering order, dialect names, escaping, literals
  src/cypher_dsl/clauses/       clause order and clause-local placement
  src/cypher_dsl/expressions/   function names, operators and predicates
  src/cypher_dsl/patterns/      pattern identity, direction and chains
  src/cypher_dsl/statements.py  finalisation, unions and decorations

Modules that exist only for this implementation include the error types,
render/bindings.py, render/capabilities.py and the comparison and traversal helpers in
syntax.py.

Ported tests

Many test scenarios and their expected Cypher come from the upstream test suite. Where a
Python test module was traced to a specific upstream test file, the module names that file
in a comment at the top. Modules without that comment hold contracts for this
implementation, and their derivation was not traced.

Changes to the derived material

  - Java source and tests are translated to Python. The public surface is built from
    factory functions, Python operators and keyword arguments, as recorded in
    docs/adr/0002-port-vocabulary-not-java-api.md.
  - Tests are rewritten for pytest. JUnit, AssertJ and generated model support are not
    carried over.
  - Rendering that intentionally differs is stated beside the expectation that pins it,
    rather than left implicit.

